# Input
```js
/* should generate diagnostics */
import { defineComponent } from "vue";

export default defineComponent({
  computed: {
    total() {
      return 1 + 2;
    },
  },
  methods: {
    log() {
      console.log(this.total());
    },
  },
});

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-define-component.js:12:19 lint/nursery/noVueComputedPropertyCall ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × The computed property total is called like a method, but its value is not a function.
  
    10 │   methods: {
    11 │     log() {
  > 12 │       console.log(this.total());
       │                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^
    13 │     },
    14 │   },
  
  i Vue gives you the value that the getter of a computed property returns. Calling a value that is not a function throws an error when the code runs.
  
  i Remove the parentheses and the arguments to read the value of the computed property.
  
